  - variational quantum circuits
  - quantum Fisher information
abstract: >
  PIQNN-Grid introduces a physics-informed learning framework in which a
  parameterized quantum circuit, rather than a classical network, is trained
  against a physics-informed loss built directly from Kirchhoff's Laws and
  the multi-machine swing equations, for real-time power-grid transient
  stability assessment. The manuscript reports results on both a fully
  simulated benchmark and an independently built pipeline evaluated against
  real IEEE 9-, 14-, and 30-bus MATPOWER case data.
